A||||3||blakeinspace||Fischer Body Sill clean-up?||||1||
Z||000000||blakeinspace||12-23-2001||03:39 PM||||Any ideas on ways to remove shallow scratches/smudges, and restore a nice shine to the plastic tabs?<P>------------------<BR>Even a stopped clock is right twice a day.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||12-23-2001||03:48 PM||||You mean the snap in logo parts?<P>On small stuff... Variable speed dremel tool with buffing wheel and compound should help. Try it on the back of one first. Keep the tool speed low for better control.<P>The lettering on them is cast in. at least on all the ones I've seen. You can tell for sure by looking at the back.||||reg||1
Z||000002||blakeinspace||12-23-2001||03:53 PM||||Ahhh yes Ogre.  Your knowledge is boundless.  Do I need some sort of compound on the buffing wheel like Soft Scrub or somesuch?  I don't want to add more scratches than are already there....<P>------------------<BR>Even a stopped clock is right twice a day.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||12-23-2001||04:52 PM||||I know Dremel, and I think Black & Decker, has polishing compound for those tools. If you have the tool but not the polishing stuff, the sets where you get the arbors, buffers and compound are usually the better deal. You can get just the compound if you have buffers.<P>When using any wheel, Dremel or bench grinder size, you want to use actual polishing compounds... using something like soft scrub or other products can have wierd results. Just for example, I tried to use Mother's with a Dremel to clean some aluminum stuff once... didn't work at all, just left a mess. At least it didn't do any damage.<P>Dremel and B&D accessories look pretty much identical and should interchange. B&D accesories are usually better cost or more product for the same cost so I'd give both a look.<P>You can see what Dremel offers at <A HREF="http://www.dremel.com" TARGET=_blank>www.dremel.com</A>  I find it just as quick to check K/Wall mart as anything. Both usually have more of each in stock than most home improvment stores or even Sears.||||reg||1
